<section>
  <section id="clavier">
    <h1>Keyboard access</h1>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Everything must be usable with the keyboard</h2>
    <p>Test with TAB and ENTER</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Is the focus visible?</h2>
    <p>
      Does the focus remain visible the entire time you're tabbing through a
      website? (<a href="https://www.dreamland.be/e/nl/dl">-</a> /{' '}
      <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/planning/statements/">+</a>)
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Focus style</h2>
    <p>Do NOT remove it:</p>
    <pre data-trim><code is:raw>a:focus { outline: none }</code></pre>
    <p>Enhance it:</p>
    <pre
      data-trim><code is:raw>a:focus { color: #fff; background: #00F; }</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Can you access everything on the website?</h2>
    <p>Can all links, form fields and buttons be reached with TAB?</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <ul>
      <li>div or span with onClick is not focusable!</li>
      <li>
        Only real links, buttons and form elements are accessible with TAB
      </li>
      <li>
        Example: try to reach the button 'extra websites' on the website of the
        town of{' '}
        <a target="tweede" href="https://www.dilbeek.be/">
          Dilbeek
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        Always use an <code is:raw>a href</code> or <code is:raw>button</code>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>JS event handlers</h2>
    <p>Prefer device independent event handlers</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Mouse dependent event handlers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>OnMouseOver</li>
      <li>onMouseOUt</li>
      <li>onDblClick</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Keyboard dependent event handlers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>onKeyDown</li>
      <li>onKeyUp</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Device independent event handlers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>onFocus</li>
      <li>onBlur</li>
      <li>onSelect</li>
      <li>onChange</li>
      <li>onClick on link or form element</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Is the TAB order logical?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Tab order = sequence of elements in source code</li>
      <li>Tab order usually corresponds to visual layout</li>
      <li>If source code is in logical order , tabbing order will be OK</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Exception: cookie banner</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Usually an overlay</li>
      <li>User wants to pass the cookie banner fast</li>
      <li>Place the cookiebanner at the top of the source code</li>
      <li>
        Example{' '}
        <a target="tweede" href="https://www.engie.be/nl/">
          -
        </a>
        /{' '}
        <a target="tweede" href="https://www.proximus.be/nl/personal/?">
          +
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>
      <code is:raw>tabindex</code>
    </h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Influences TAB sequence</li>
      <li>Only to be used in specific cases</li>
      <li>Only use values 0 and -1</li>
      <li>Tabindex > 0 changes keyboard sequence but not reading order</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>
      <code is:raw>tabindex="0"</code>
    </h2>
    <ul>
      <li>adds non focusable element (div or span) in tab sequence</li>
      <li>Can be useful when building widgets</li>
      <li>
        Example:{' '}
        <a
          target="tweede"
          href="https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-practices-1.1/#tabpanel">
          tabs
        </a>{' '}
        or custom checkbox
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>
      <code is:raw>tabindex="-1"</code>
    </h2>
    <ul>
      <li>removes a focusable element from the TAB sequence</li>
      <li>Makes an element focusable via javascript</li>
      <li>Example: Modal dialog or same page link</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Manage focus properly</h2>

    <p>Behaviour should be predictable</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Clicking on a link generally moves the focus (whether page load or not)
      </li>
      <li>Clicking on a button sometimes moves the focus, sometimes not</li>
      <li>
        Interacting with a form field (checkbox, dropdown) should not move the
        focus
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Can you use all of the site's features?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Can links be activated with <strong>ENTER</strong>?
      </li>
      <li>
        Can radio buttons be selected with the <strong>SPACE bar</strong>?
      </li>
      <li>
        Can buttons be activated using <strong>SPACE bar</strong> or{' '}
        <strong>ENTER</strong>?
      </li>
      <li>
        Can lists be navigated with the <strong>ARROW keys</strong>?
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Keyboard interaction</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Always works with <strong>native HTML</strong> when possible: a, button,
        input, select, list,...
      </li>
      <li>
        Custom-made widgets and forms: all accessibility has to be manually
        coded by you
      </li>
      <li>
        Follow the{' '}
        <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-practices/">
          Authoring Practices
        </a>{' '}
        to ensure consistency
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Other keyboard-related topics</h2>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Skiplinks</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Useful for complex navigations</li>

      <li>
        <a target="tweede" href="https://www.kobavision.be">
          Don't overdo it
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Keyboard trap</h2>
    <p>Avoid getting stuck in a focus loop, e.g. forms or lists</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Keyboard shortcuts</h2>
    <p>
      When adding shortcuts, they should not override the user's own keyboard
      shortcuts.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Allow the user to turn them off</li>
      <li>Allow the user to redefine them</li>
      <li>
        Make shortcuts available only when their corresponding element is
        focused
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Example</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>YouTube: videos can be paused with the character "K"</li>
      <li>
        This shortcut only works when the video has focus, but not anywhere else
        on the page
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</section>
